NATIONAT ASSEM BLY SECRETARIAT
ORDERS OF THE DAYfor the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Thursday, the 15th January ,2025 a102.00 p.m.1, Tilawot, Hodith, Noot and national anthem.QUESTIONS2. Questions entered in a separate list to be asked and answers given.CATTING ATTENTION NOTICE
3. MS. SHARMILA SAHIBA FARUQUI HASHAAM MR. KHURSHID AHMED JUNEJOMIRZA IKHTIAR BAIG MR. RAMESH tAL to invite attentionof the Minister for Commerce to a matter of urgent public importance regarding serious disruptions inrice exports from Pakistan to European countries resulting loss to the exchequer, causing graveconcern amongst the public.MOTION
4. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAQ DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Mlnister for Foreign Affairs tomove under rule 288 of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the National Assembly,2007 that the requirement of sub-rule (2) of rule 123 of the said rules be suspended in order to takeinto consideration the Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation | 8il1,2024.
TEGISTATIVE BUSINESS
5. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAQ DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Minister for Foreign Affairs tomove that the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Development, Productionand Stockpiling of Bacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weapons and on their Destruction, 7972 lTheBiological and Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation ) B'il, 2024), as reported by the StandingCommittee, be taken into consideration at once.
6. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAQ DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Minister for Foreign Affairs tomove that the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Development, Productionand Stockpiling of Bacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weapons and on their Destruction, 7972 [TheBiological and Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation I B;il!,20241, be passed.
MATTERS OTHER THAN POINTS OF ORDER
Raising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points of OrderCALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
8. MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to invite attention of the Minister for National HealthServices, Regulations and Coordination to a matter of urgent public importance regarding shortage ofmedical equipment, including essential items like ventilators, testing machines and GeneXpertsystems, in PIMS, lslamabad, the Federal Government Polyclinic, lslamabad and other federallyadministered hospitals, causing grave concern amongst the public.
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
7.
lslamabad, the15th Januarv, 2025

